      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "In a previous systematic review, Gomez-Ochoa et al revealed the lack of PPE, patient contact, and suboptimal hand hygiene as risk factors for COVID-19 among HCWs [12]. However, no meta-analysis was conducted. Furthermore, Chou et al, living rapid review focused on a broad range of coronavirus infections... Only 3 studies included reported risk factors for SARS-CoV-2 infections among health workers.",
      "reason": "The Introduction describes the existing evidence base (prior reviews by Gomez-Ochoa et al and Chou et al) and identifies gaps/uncertainties, such as the absence of meta-analysis and the limited number of studies on SARS-CoV-2 risk factors among HCWs."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_8",
      "quote": "To better inform occupational health policy and map available evidence on the COVID-19 risk factors among HCWs, we conducted a systematic review and meta-analysis to summarize and critically analyze the existing evidence on SARS-CoV-2 risk factors among HCWs. Given the dynamic nature of the COVID-19 pandemic, there is an urgent need to continuously review the literature and update the aggregated",
      "reason": "The importance and need for the review are explicitly explained: informing occupational health policy, mapping evidence, and the urgent need for continuous updating given the dynamic pandemic."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "In a previous systematic review, Gomez-Ochoa et al revealed the lack of PPE, patient contact, and suboptimal hand hygiene as risk factors for COVID-19 among HCWs [12]. However, no meta-analysis was conducted. Furthermore, Chou et al, living rapid review focused on a broad range of coronavirus infections.",
      "reason": "Similar existing systematic reviews are identified and cited (Gomez-Ochoa et al [12]; Chou et al [13]), and the need for the current review is justified by their limitations (no meta-analysis; broad focus with only 3 SARS-CoV-2 risk factor studies)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "This is a review of risk factors for COVID-19 infection, not a review of intervention effects, so no mechanism of action of an intervention needs to be described."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "This is an etiological review of risk factors, not a review of complex interventions or delivery contexts, so a logic model is not required."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 90
}

